1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,765
Chapter-15. 
Ethan Bruce POV

2
00:00:02,765 --> 00:00:07,242
The penthouse was soundproof-a specification I'd insisted upon when I bought it.

3
00:00:07,242 --> 00:00:09,792
Tonight, it proved to be a very good investment.

4
00:00:09,792 --> 00:00:12,109
Leo Vance was no longer a Capo.

5
00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:16,552
He was a heap of broken bones and bloody regret smeared across the designer rug.

6
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:17,888
I hadn't used a gun.

7
00:00:17,888 --> 00:00:20,279
A gun was too quick.A gun was mercy.

8
00:00:20,279 --> 00:00:21,856
Instead, I used my fists.

9
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:23,989
I used the heavy crystal ashtray.

10
00:00:23,989 --> 00:00:26,340
I used the crushing weight of my boot heel.

11
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:29,752
Every time I heard a bone snap, I saw Aurora falling.

12
00:00:29,752 --> 00:00:30,224
Snap.

13
00:00:30,224 --> 00:00:31,818
That was for her broken arm.

14
00:00:31,818 --> 00:00:32,354
Snap.

15
00:00:32,354 --> 00:00:33,950
That was for her bruised ribs.

16
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:34,386
Snap.

17
00:00:34,386 --> 00:00:38,057
That was for the sheer terror she felt when the van door closed.

18
00:00:38,057 --> 00:00:40,502
Leo had stopped moving ten minutes ago.

19
00:00:40,502 --> 00:00:42,561
He was still breathing, but barely.

20
00:00:42,561 --> 00:00:44,092
He would never walk again.

21
00:00:44,092 --> 00:00:45,869
He would never hold a gun again.

22
00:00:45,869 --> 00:00:49,466
I wiped my crimson-stained hands on his ruined silk shirt.

23
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,174
Then, I turned to Ilene.

24
00:00:51,174 --> 00:00:56,243
She hadn't moved.She was huddled in the corner, her makeup running down her face in black streaks.

25
00:00:56,243 --> 00:00:58,267
She looked like a weeping gargoyle.

26
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:02,629
"Ethan," she whimpered."I'm sorry.I'm sick.You know I'm sick.My father..."

27
00:01:02,629 --> 00:01:03,674
"Don't," I said.

28
00:01:03,674 --> 00:01:06,331
The mention of her father usually made me pause.

29
00:01:06,331 --> 00:01:08,953
It usually made the guilt rise up and choke me.

30
00:01:08,953 --> 00:01:09,708
But today?

31
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:11,317
Today, I felt nothing.

32
00:01:11,317 --> 00:01:15,687
"Your father was a soldier," I said, my voice low as I stalked toward her.

33
00:01:15,687 --> 00:01:17,516
"He died taking a bullet for me.

34
00:01:17,516 --> 00:01:18,814
He died with honor."

35
00:01:18,814 --> 00:01:21,478
I stopped in front of her.I towered over her.

36
00:01:21,478 --> 00:01:22,486
"You have none."

37
00:01:22,486 --> 00:01:24,099
"I love you!" she shrieked.

38
00:01:24,099 --> 00:01:25,821
"I did it because I love you!"

39
00:01:25,821 --> 00:01:27,287
"You don't love me," I spat.

40
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:29,503
"You love the power.You love the money.

41
00:01:29,503 --> 00:01:32,542
You love that I was the only one who couldn't say no to you."

42
00:01:32,542 --> 00:01:36,007
I reached down, tangling my fingers in her hair, and yanked.

43
00:01:36,007 --> 00:01:37,008
She screamed.

44
00:01:37,008 --> 00:01:38,792
I pulled her roughly to her feet.

45
00:01:38,792 --> 00:01:41,197
"You are a traitor to this Family," I said.

46
00:01:41,197 --> 00:01:45,225
"You conspired with a rival Capo to harm the wife of the Underboss."

47
00:01:45,225 --> 00:01:46,747
"I'm a Ward!" she cried.

48
00:01:46,747 --> 00:01:48,272
"You swore to protect me!"

49
00:01:48,272 --> 00:01:50,573
"I swore to protect Ilene Wolf," I said.

50
00:01:50,573 --> 00:01:51,960
"The daughter of a hero."

51
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,542
I dragged her toward the door.

52
00:01:53,542 --> 00:01:54,702
"That woman is dead.

53
00:01:54,702 --> 00:01:57,564
You killed her the moment you sold my wife to a monster."

54
00:01:57,564 --> 00:02:00,290
She clawed at my hands.She kicked.She bit.

55
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:01,235
It didn't matter.

56
00:02:01,235 --> 00:02:02,826
I was done being gentle.

57
00:02:02,826 --> 00:02:05,835
I was done being the man who tried to balance the scales.

58
00:02:05,835 --> 00:02:07,231
The scales were broken.

59
00:02:07,231 --> 00:02:10,863
I dragged her into the elevator and pressed the button for the garage.

60
00:02:10,863 --> 00:02:12,614
"Where are we going?" she sobbed.

61
00:02:12,614 --> 00:02:14,503
"Ethan, please, don't kill me."

62
00:02:14,503 --> 00:02:17,391
I looked at her reflection in the polished metal doors.

63
00:02:17,391 --> 00:02:21,070
"Death is easy, Ilene," I said, my eyes locking with hers.

64
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,443
"You don't get off that easy."
